      "answer": "$\\frac\\pi2-\\ln2$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Commence integration and reach $ax\\tan^{-1}(\\frac12x)+b\\int\\frac{x}{c+x^2}\\,dx$ - *M1; OE; denominator may be $1+x^2/4$ or $2+x^2/2$. Obtain $x\\tan^{-1}(\\frac12x)-\\int\\frac{2x}{4+x^2}\\,dx$ - A1; OE. Complete integration to $x\\tan^{-1}(\\frac12x)-\\ln(4+x^2)$ - A1; OE, e.g. with $\\ln(1+x^2/4)$. Substitute limits correctly in $px\\tan^{-1}x+q\\ln(c+x^2)$ - DM1; e.g. $2\\tan^{-1}1-\\ln8+\\ln4$. Obtain $\\frac\\pi2-\\ln2$ - A1; exact answer, requiring a value for $\\tan^{-1}1$ and one logarithm term. Alternative substitution $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}(x/2)$: obtain $\\lambda\\int2\\theta\\sec^2\\theta\\,d\\theta$ and reach $p\\theta\\tan\\theta+q\\int\\tan\\theta\\,d\\theta$ - *M1; obtain $2\\theta\\tan\\theta-2\\int\\tan\\theta\\,d\\theta$ - A1; complete to $2\\theta\\tan\\theta+2\\ln(\\cos\\theta)$ - A1; substitute limits $\\pi/4$ and 0 correctly - DM1; limits must be in radians. Obtain $\\frac\\pi2-\\ln2$ - A1. Total: 5.",
